   "final_text": "Everything in the feed is handled, and the feed has had no new events for about 50 minutes.\n\n**What happened:** The feed had three events, and two of them were one change. Kofi Silva went from contractor (C5001) to employee (E1023), both effective 2026-11-02. I checked he's the same person: the new record lists C5001 as its contractor origin, and both records carry the same government ID token. Policy says to carry the identity over on a conversion, so I moved his existing account to the new record rather than shutting it down.\n\n**Termination of C5001 (seq 1):**\n- **Kept on purpose:** his account `acct-1a16daff` stays enabled, with no sessions cut off and no licence, mailbox or group removals. He has no legal hold.\n- **Skipped because he's staying:** no request to get his laptop back, no final pay and no expense-report closure. His corporate card was already inactive.\n- **Left open:** one expense report on the old record, exp-2e87d415 for 988, is waiting for approval from his manager, Jordan Carter. Jordan is still active, so the report should be approved through the normal process. I didn't reroute or close it.\n\n**Hire of E1023 (seq 3):**\n- **Account:** `acct-1a16daff` is now linked to the new record as an Employee. It keeps the same login and email (kofi.silva@example.com) and his existing access groups (All-Staff, Eng-Git, VPN-Users), which match what the Software Engineer role gets by default.\n- **Finance:** I created a profile with cost center CC-1000 and Jordan Carter as expense approver.\n- **Work email:** I wrote it back to Workday and confirmed it saved. The confirmation event (seq 2) was just the result of that update.\n- **Onboarding tasks:** I marked \"Create accounts and email\" complete. I also marked \"Provision equipment\" complete without ordering anything new, because his engineering kit from his contractor time (tkt-eq-C5001) was already delivered and stays with him. If he should get a fresh equipment order as a new employee, that needs to be placed separately.\n\nNothing I started is still pending, and I didn't need to escalate anything."
